This confirms the exact defect: `bp->b_mxfs_sync_wait` is a per-buffer field that gets unconditionally overwritten by *any* call to `xfs_buf_submit()`, so xfsaild's concurrent async resubmission clobbers rm's sync-wait latch before rm's own completion arrives — neither of the two existing override checks can fire because the field they check has already been stomped to 0. Let me read the actual `xfs_buf_iowait()` function to design a targeted, safe fix per the escape-hatch approach the project's own prior investigation already recommended.
Let me check the completion code around the override checks (what the async branch actually does when it *doesn't* fire the override) and the caller-side relse in `mxfs_dir_data_owner_scan`, to make sure a fix doesn't introduce a double-release.
